{#
  The library create form.

  The only create page whose form is library-scoped but carries **no library**: the record
  being created is the library. `Books\Service\LibraryFormFactory` handles that with
  `if (isset($libraryId))`, so `mainCollectionId` renders with no options — a library that
  does not exist yet has no collections. App\Books\LibraryScopedForms::formForLibrary()
  reproduces the same skip.

  The create page is the edit page with a different heading, a different action and no
  record — which is exactly what laminas says too: create.phtml and edit.phtml are separate
  view scripts that include the same fields-partial.phtml. So this template **extends its
  edit twin** and overrides only what differs. What that inherits is the page's assets and
  its inline scripts, which on laminas come from the shared partial rather than from either
  view script, so inheriting them is the faithful arrangement rather than a shortcut.
#}
{% extends 'books/library-edit.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Create new library') }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('books/_library-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_submit(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
